        "title": "Aquatic Food Webs: Trophic Cascades, Keystone Species, Bioaccumulation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Freshwater food webs are controlled both from the bottom up (nutrient availability controlling algal production → herbivore → predator) and from the top down (apex predators controlling prey and indirectly controlling lower trophic levels). The Carpenter lake experiments established that top-down control is often decisive in lakes — a result with direct management implications."
    },
