      },
      "text": "```\n  LAKE CHARACTERISTICS FAVORING STRONG CASCADES:\n  +-- Planktonic system: phytoplankton and zooplankton are mobile and responsive\n  +-- Few species at each trophic level: less redundancy, stronger per-species effect\n  +-- Daphnia is highly effective grazer: can clear an entire epilimnion\n  +-- Closed basin: cascade effects not diluted by flow from upstream\n  +-- Short generation times: rapid population responses to predator change"
